{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And he entreated Him, etc.</b> The reason it did not say ״וַיֵּדַע יִצְחָק אֶת״ etc., as it says (Genesis 4:1) ״וְהָאָדָם יָדַע״, (I Samuel 1:19) ״וַיֵּדַע אֶלְקָנָה״ etc. — perhaps it is because the prayer was after he had relations with her, within the first three days, as they of blessed memory said (Berakhot 60a) that during the first three days one should pray that it not putrefy — and this was the prayer of Yitzchak."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:43:15.053831847Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}